fix(newpolka): sort the rows in a logarithmic stack depth

The quicksort of the rows of matrices recursed on both parts: on large,
unbalanced matrices (relations between all the variables of a C+Python
analysis), its depth grows with the number of rows and exhausts the stack
of a wasm worker. It now recurses on the smaller part and loops on the
larger one. The rows end in the same order.

